steps.say:
Here is a loop inside a loop. The inner loop’s limit is i, so it changes from row to row.
for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
        System.out.print("#");
    }
    System.out.println();
}
Rule one: for each single pass of the outer loop, the inner loop runs all the way from its start to its end.

beats.code:
for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
        System.out.print("#");
    }
    System.out.println();
}

